Origin of the costing logic
---------------------------
The rules for reading Claude Code transcripts, counting tokens per message,
splitting cache writes and fast mode, matching paths and worktrees to a
repository, finding ticket keys and pricing tokens were first written by PWW
for OneDroid Talos (providentiaww/talosdashboard, src/costs and
src/session/transcripts.js). That code is PWW's own and carries no licence
file of its own.

Per Michal Bacia's decision of 2026-10-21, PWW relicenses that costing logic
under the Apache License, Version 2.0, for use in OneDroid Valor.

The Go code in this repository is a clean rewrite: no JavaScript source was
copied. Talos's test vectors were ported as Go table tests, and the parity
fixtures under testdata/ are generated, with no real transcript content.

The seed price list (internal/prices/prices.json) restates the vendors'
published list prices as read on the date in each entry.

Origin of the record format and the credential rules
----------------------------------------------------
The record format (record/) and the credential rules (redact/) were first
written by PWW for the OneDroid Synapse recorder (providentiaww/MCP-router,
internal/agentrecord/contract and internal/agentrecord/secrets). That code is
PWW's own and carries no licence file of its own.

Per Michal Bacia's decision of 2026-11-07 (D41a), PWW relicenses it under the
Apache License, Version 2.0, for the OneDroid Argus kit. The packages here are
a rewrite that keeps the record's wire format byte-compatible with the
recorder, so both write the same rows. Test fixtures that look like real
credentials are synthetic and split in the source.
